{"school":{"dbn":"25Q164","name":"P.S. 164 Queens Valley","boro":"Queens","district":"25","district_label":"District 25","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":528,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"138-01 77 AVENUE, QUEENS, NY 11367","phone":"7184453232","website":"HTTPS://WWW.PSMS164.ORG/","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/65971","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"At Queens Valley School of the Arts, our mission is to inspire, nurture, and develop the creative potential of all our students through a high-quality, standards-based curriculum infused with the arts. We are dedicated to leveraging the interests and talents of our students while addressing each child's academic, social, and developmental needs.  The Queens Valley School of the Arts community believes that our students have the right to a comprehensive instructional program that will prepare them to reach their fullest potential. Our goal is to develop students who are independent thinkers with a strong knowledge of the arts, motivated to achieve new heights in both their academic and creative endeavors.   We offer a unique Talent program that allows students to delve deeply into visual arts, dance, drama, vocal and instrumental music, and publishing.  This vibrant program encourages creativity and provides an enriched learning environment through our many partnerships with NYC premiere cultural institutions.  Our teachers partner with organizations including The Met, Morgan Library, Education through Music, the Noel Pointer Foundation, NYC Press Pass and Ajna Dance Company to name a few.   Queens Valley School prides itself on providing a dedicated staff and a small school environment that fosters individualized support across social, emotional, and academic spheres and ensuring that every student has the opportunity to succeed and grow in a supportive and dynamic environment.","start_tim